WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.912 --> 00:00:16.880
The next day Mother stayed in bed because her head ached so badly.

2
00:00:17.920 --> 00:00:20.142
She had a fever and would not eat anything.

3
00:00:21.182 --> 00:00:23.524
Dr. Forest came and said it was the flu.

4
00:00:23.544 --> 00:00:27.746
"Nurse Bobbie," the doctor said, smiling at Bobbie.

5
00:00:27.766 --> 00:00:31.108
"I'll send some medicine later.

6
00:00:31.992 --> 00:00:37.537
Please give your mother this list—she needs beef soup, fresh fruit, and brandy."

7
00:00:38.658 --> 00:00:41.880
When the doctor had gone, Bobbie showed Mother the piece of paper.

8
00:00:41.900 --> 00:00:45.503
"Impossible!" Mother said with a laugh.

9
00:00:45.523 --> 00:00:48.766
"We can't buy all these things!

10
00:00:49.667 --> 00:00:51.068
We're poor, remember?"

11
00:00:51.088 --> 00:00:54.651
"Yes, Mother," Bobbie answered and tried to smile.

12
00:00:55.652 --> 00:00:56.713
The children talked later.

13
00:00:56.733 --> 00:01:01.416
"Mother needs those things," said Bobbie.

14
00:01:01.436 --> 00:01:02.797
"How can we get them for her?

15
00:01:03.877 --> 00:01:06.299
Think, everybody, as hard as you can."

16
00:01:09.340 --> 00:01:10.241
A plan was formed.

17
00:01:11.341 --> 00:01:15.083
Phyllis and Peter found a white sheet, some black paint, and a paintbrush.

18
00:01:16.124 --> 00:01:17.865
Bobbie stayed with Mother all night long.

19
00:01:18.885 --> 00:01:20.486
The next morning the doctor came again.

20
00:01:20.506 --> 00:01:23.668
"Everything going all right, little nurse?"

21
00:01:24.028 --> 00:01:25.369
Dr. Forest said in the hall.

22
00:01:25.389 --> 00:01:28.711
"Did you get the brandy and fruit for your mother?"

23
00:01:28.731 --> 00:01:31.645
"No, I couldn't.

24
00:01:32.726 --> 00:01:34.607
But I'll get them tomorrow," Bobbie said.

25
00:01:34.627 --> 00:01:38.030
"Very well, then," the doctor replied.

26
00:01:40.993 --> 00:01:45.817
When the 9:15 train came out of the tunnel that same morning, the old gentleman was ready to

27
00:01:45.877 --> 00:01:50.941
wave. But instead of three children on the fence, there was just one: Peter.

28
00:01:51.982 --> 00:01:53.043
But he was not waving.

29
00:01:55.485 --> 00:01:58.908
Instead Peter was pointing at the large white sheet attached to the fence.

30
00:02:00.068 --> 00:02:03.470
On the sheet were thick black letters that read: Look Out at the Station.

31
00:02:04.770 --> 00:02:08.752
Many passengers looked out their windows at the station, but they saw nothing peculiar.

32
00:02:11.373 --> 00:02:15.414
But as the train was departing, the old gentleman saw Phyllis running toward him.

33
00:02:15.434 --> 00:02:18.396
"I thought I was going to miss you!"

34
00:02:18.856 --> 00:02:19.456
she shouted.

35
00:02:20.597 --> 00:02:24.238
She quickly thrust a letter into his hand through the window as the train moved away.

36
00:02:26.039 --> 00:02:29.765
The old gentleman relaxed in his seat and opened the letter: Dear Mr.

37
00:02:30.265 --> 00:02:32.547
(we do not know your name), Mother is ill.

38
00:02:33.707 --> 00:02:35.929
The doctor says we must give her good food.

39
00:02:37.030 --> 00:02:39.452
But we don't have any money because Father is away.

40
00:02:41.293 --> 00:02:42.053
Can you help us?

41
00:02:42.714 --> 00:02:43.595
We can repay you.

42
00:02:44.575 --> 00:02:50.900
From Roberta, Peter, and Phyllis Below their names they had written down their requests.

43
00:02:53.822 --> 00:02:56.384
That evening Perks came to their house with a big parcel.

44
00:02:57.640 --> 00:02:59.721
Inside were all the things they had asked for.

45
00:03:00.741 --> 00:03:05.702
There were also some things they had not asked for—wine, two chickens, and flowers.

46
00:03:06.823 --> 00:03:07.723
There was a letter too.

47
00:03:09.623 --> 00:03:11.984
Children, Here is the food for your mother.

48
00:03:13.204 --> 00:03:17.485
If she says you were wrong to ask for the things, tell her that I say you were

49
00:03:17.545 --> 00:03:20.106
right. I was pleased to help.

50
00:03:21.326 --> 00:03:24.147
The old man's name was underneath, but it was illegible.

51
00:03:24.167 --> 00:03:28.053
"I think we were right," said Phyllis.

52
00:03:28.073 --> 00:03:31.497
"Of course, we were right," said Bobbie.

53
00:03:31.517 --> 00:03:35.642
"I hope Mother thinks we were right too," said Peter.

54
00:03:36.723 --> 00:03:38.285
But he didn't sound very sure.
